{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained). CONFIRMED LIVE FAILURE. :89 reads .env-id and :35/:170/:268 read+write last-pass.json from repo_root/.tickets-tracker; routed both through config.tracker_dir() via the new _store_dir() helper, and DETAIL_RELATIVE became DETAIL_IN_STORE (relative to the resolved store, not the repo root)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained). :601 load_binding_store composed the pass's entire binding read/write root from the literal; now resolved through config.tracker_dir(repo_root). Module docstring retitled to <store>/.bridge_state/bindings.json."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained, 2 sites). :318 wrote prev_snapshot.json and seeded ctx.tracker_dir; :456 check_store_compat validated the wrong store before Jira mutations. Both now go through the new _tracker_dir() resolver wrapper, and the stale :452 comment asserting the boundary was deliberate is removed."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained). :321 wrote BRIDGE_ALERT events into repo_root/.tickets-tracker, materializing a shadow store when relocated; now resolved via config.tracker_dir()."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/git_adapter.py","reason":"LEGITIMATE USE (sanctioned, value PRESERVED). :75 TRACKER_DIR is a committed-TREE pathspec label on the tickets branch, not an on-disk store root, and is exported in __all__ + pinned by a characterization test. Relocation does not rename it. Comment rewritten and given a reason-bearing tickets-boundary-ok marker; only its consumer in reconcile_helpers.py was changed."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained). :234 consumed git_adapter.TRACKER_DIR as repo_root/TRACKER_DIR to stage the binding-store commit-back; the ON-DISK root is now resolved through config.tracker_dir() while TRACKER_DIR stays the committed-tree pathspec label."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained). :47 _projects_path read+write of the sync mapping was asymmetric with _lib_ops, which commits the correctly resolved tracker. Now resolved via a function-body rebar.config import so the module's stdlib-only module level (required by the by-path spec loaders) is preserved."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained). :165 honoured REBAR_TRACKER_DIR but ignored the tracker.dir config key; the hand-rolled helper body is replaced by a direct delegation to config.tracker_dir(), which carries the full precedence."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained, 2 sites). :239 reconcile-check loaded local tickets from the literal; :508 dry-run enumeration silently returned 0 on a relocated store. Both now call config.tracker_dir()."},{"path":"src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained). :180 passed a RELATIVE --tracker .tickets-tracker to the delivery subprocess run with cwd=repo_root, so a relocated deployment delivered into <root>/.tickets-tracker; _delivery_command now takes root and passes the resolved ABSOLUTE config.tracker_dir(root)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py","reason":"GENUINE BYPASS (drained). :663 CLI fallback arm honoured the env override but ignored the tracker.dir config key, so fsck audited the wrong path; the override branch is collapsed into config.tracker_dir(repo_root)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","reason":"LEGITIMATE USE (sanctioned, unchanged behaviour). The literal here is the ConfigError-only fallback INSIDE the read-path resolver tracker_dir() itself: REBAR_TRACKER_DIR has already returned above and an absolute tracker.dir returns verbatim below, so a relocated store never reaches this branch. Given a reason-bearing tickets-boundary-ok marker plus an explanatory comment."},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"LEGITIMATE USE (sanctioned, unchanged behaviour). The literal is the ConfigError-only default INSIDE config.tracker_dir() — the resolver that APPLIES relocation. Only an unparseable config reaches it, and then no configured value exists. Given a reason-bearing tickets-boundary-ok marker plus an explanatory comment."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"LEGITIMATE USE (sanctioned, unchanged behaviour). :317 in denied_paths() the literal is a denylist SUPERSET entry; the CONFIGURED store is appended just below via _root_config.tracker_dir(root), so relocation IS honoured and keeping the default name can only deny MORE paths, never leave a relocated store unprotected. Given a reason-bearing tickets-boundary-ok marker."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py","reason":"LEGITIMATE USE (sanctioned, unchanged behaviour). :253 the literal is the COMPARISON SUBJECT of the dir-mismatch hint — the branch exists to warn that tracker.dir was pointed AWAY from the default while a store still sits at the default name, so resolving it would compare the resolved tracker to itself. Given a reason-bearing tickets-boundary-ok marker."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","reason":"LEGITIMATE USE (sanctioned, unchanged behaviour). _TRACKER_DIRNAME names a directory inside the snapshot root THIS module creates, deliberately the default name so the materialized root resolves through config.tracker_dir(<that root>) onto it. Relocation moves the OPERATOR's store, not a synthesized snapshot. Comment rewritten with a reason-bearing marker."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_view.py","reason":"LEGITIMATE USE (sanctioned, unchanged behaviour). :73 is a scratch dir inside the mkdtemp() created on the preceding line — a private throwaway view root nothing outside the object reads. Honouring a relocation here would point the scratch view at the LIVE store, the opposite of the intent. Given a reason-bearing tickets-boundary-ok marker."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py","reason":"LEGITIMATE USE (sanctioned, unchanged behaviour). _DEFAULT_TRACKER_DIR is consumed only by _resolve_tracker_dir in the same module, as the absent-key default when the captured config snapshot carries no tracker.dir; every relocation is applied there. Given a reason-bearing tickets-boundary-ok marker."},{"path":"scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py","reason":"NEW. AC4 gate: AST-based, rejects new store-path COMPOSITION from the hardcoded literal in src/ (a / join, an os.path.join/Path(...) argument, or a name bound to the bare dir name), leaving all 55 docstring/comment/help-text occurrences untouched. Enforces the previously unenforced # tickets-boundary-ok convention with a MANDATORY reason — the bare marker had become a rubber stamp, carried by 7 of the 13 defects."},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"Wire the new check_tickets_boundary.py gate into make lint alongside the sibling repo gates."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_relocated_store.py","reason":"NEW. RED-first regression test: bridge_status against a store relocated outside the repo root via REBAR_TRACKER_DIR — the exact live failure (.env-id read at an unconfigured path) this ticket was filed for."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_tickets_boundary_guard.py","reason":"NEW. Gate self-tests for check_tickets_boundary.py, following the existing check_* guard test pattern: composition detected, prose/comments ignored, bare marker rejected, reason-bearing marker accepted."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py","reason":"Test-fixture follow-on, not a boundary site: the new gate is wired into make lint AHEAD of the guard under test, so this test's synthetic scripts/ dir needs a stub check_tickets_boundary.py for the same reason it already stubs its siblings."},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"Record that the tickets-boundary marker convention is now ENFORCED by a gate, with the mandatory-reason sanction form."},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Generated-inventory line-number refresh only: the explanatory comment blocks added to config.py and llm/config.py shifted the recorded os.environ.get(<non-literal>) call-site lines. No env-var semantics changed."},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"Fix entry, including the deliberate NO-MIGRATION note: nothing reads <repo_root>/.tickets-tracker after this change, so residue a relocated deployment already wrote there is inert rather than divergent, and deleting a directory rebar no longer interprets is left to the operator."}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1787890076097995930,"uuid":"ae3ab0fd-4195-447c-9935-31f1a2a64737"}